---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
export const prerender = true;
const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const lastUpdated = "May 15, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service — Tape"
  description="The rules of the road for using tape.io — what the site is, what it isn't, and what we expect from each other."
>
  <article class="legal-root">
    <p class="legal-eyebrow">Terms</p>
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p class="lead">
      By using tape.io you agree to these terms. They're
      short on purpose. The whole document is in plain English and
      should take about three minutes to read.
    </p>

    <h2>What this is</h2>

    <p>
      Tape is an editorial dashboard for public financial
      and macroeconomic data — a way to see, save, and share charts of
      indicators like inflation, employment, market prices, GDP,
      federal spending, and similar series. Underlying data comes from
      public providers (FRED, Yahoo Finance, BLS, OECD, World Bank, US
      Treasury, USAspending, Census). Each chart cites its source.
    </p>

    <h2>What this is NOT</h2>

    <p>
      <strong>Not investment advice.</strong> Nothing on the site is a
      recommendation to buy, sell, or hold any security, currency,
      commodity, or other instrument. The data is illustrative and
      educational; it's not actionable.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Not real-time.</strong> Most data is refreshed weekly via
      a scheduled pipeline. Some series additionally lag the underlying
      provider by days, weeks, or quarters depending on their release
      cadence. Treat everything as historical, not live.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Not authoritative.</strong> I work to fetch accurate
      data, but errors happen — bad provider releases, broken
      pipelines, my own bugs. Always cross-check with the original
      source (linked in every chart's footer) before relying on a
      specific number for anything that matters. The site is provided
      "as-is" with no warranty of accuracy.
    </p>

    <h2>Your account</h2>

    <p>
      You can use much of the site without an account — preset
      dashboards, shared URLs, and the composer's URL-state mode all
      work for anonymous visitors. Signing in (Google OAuth) lets you
      save dashboards to your account at <code>/u/&lt;slug&gt;/</code>.
      You're responsible for activity under your account; if you
      suspect unauthorized access, email me.
    </p>

    <p>
      I can suspend or terminate accounts that abuse the service:
      bot-driven traffic, attempts to evade the rate limits, spam
      submissions, sharing manifestly harmful or unlawful content via
      custom dashboard titles or notes, and similar bad-faith use.
    </p>

    <h2>Your content</h2>

    <p>
      You retain ownership of any content you create on the site —
      saved-dashboard titles, descriptions, written notes, and the
      compositions themselves. By saving a dashboard publicly (the
      default), you grant me a non-exclusive license to host and
      display it to anyone who visits its URL. By marking it private,
      you restrict that license to display only to your signed-in
      account.
    </p>

    <p>
      You're responsible for what you write into your dashboards.
      Don't include other people's personal information. Don't write
      libelous content. Don't try to attack other visitors via
      malicious content. Generic civility applies.
    </p>

    <h2>The underlying data</h2>

    <p>
      The numerical data is owned by its original providers (FRED,
      Yahoo Finance, BLS, OECD, World Bank, US Treasury, USAspending,
      Census, and others) and used under each provider's terms. I
      republish observations as a derivative analytical work, citing
      each original source. If you intend to use the data for
      commercial redistribution or commercial decision-making beyond
      viewing it on this site, consult the original provider's terms.
    </p>

    <p>
      This product uses the FRED&reg; API but is not endorsed or
      certified by the Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis.
    </p>

    <h2>Rate limits and fair use</h2>

    <p>
      The free tier has rate limits so the service stays usable for
      everyone:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>Email signup: up to 5 attempts per IP per day.</li>
      <li>
        Saved dashboards: limits per signed-in user (50 new saves per
        day, 300 edits per day, etc.) and per IP (100 new saves per
        IP per day) to discourage multi-account abuse.
      </li>
      <li>
        Composer: anonymous visitors get 20 chart-adds + derived-source
        creations per IP per day before being prompted to sign in.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      If you hit a limit and need higher quotas — typically because
      you're using the site at a team or organization scale — email me
      about <a href={`${baseUrl}/enterprise/`}>Enterprise Support</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Liability</h2>

    <p>
      The site is provided "as-is" and "as-available." I make no
      warranty that the data is accurate, complete, or current, or
      that the service will be uninterrupted or error-free. To the
      maximum extent permitted by law, I'm not liable for any losses
      arising from your use of the site — including, specifically,
      financial losses from trading or investment decisions you make
      based on information you saw here. Again: this isn't investment
      advice; don't trade on it.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>

    <p>
      If I change these terms, I'll update the "Last updated" date at
      the top. Significant changes (new restrictions, new account
      obligations) will be announced via email to registered users.
      Continued use of the site after a change constitutes acceptance.
    </p>

    <h2>Data takedown / removal requests</h2>

    <p>
      If you're a data provider whose series appears here and you'd
      like it removed, please email
      <a href="mailto:keller.scholl@gmail.com">keller.scholl@gmail.com</a>.
      I will remove the data promptly (target: within one business
      week) and will not require you to escalate. You don't need to
      threaten or invoke counsel — a polite request is enough.
    </p>

    <p>
      The same applies to corrections: if any series I display has
      drifted from what your source publishes, or if my attribution
      is wrong, I'd rather fix it than argue about it. Email is the
      easiest path.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact + governing law</h2>

    <p>
      Keller Scholl —
      <a href="mailto:keller.scholl@gmail.com">keller.scholl@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of the District of Columbia,
      United States. Any dispute will be resolved in the state or
      federal courts located in the District of Columbia.
    </p>

    <p class="footer-note">
      <a href={baseUrl || "/"}>&larr; All dashboards</a>
      ·
      <a href={`${baseUrl}/privacy/`}>Privacy Policy</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-root {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 64px 24px 96px;
    color: var(--color-neutral-900);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .legal-eyebrow {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--color-neutral-500);
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  .legal-root h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }
  .legal-updated {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-neutral-500);
    margin: 0 0 32px;
  }
  .legal-root h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 40px 0 8px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-neutral-500);
  }
  .legal-root p,
  .legal-root ul {
    margin: 12px 0;
    color: var(--color-neutral-700);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
  }
  .legal-root ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  .legal-root li {
    margin: 6px 0;
  }
  .legal-root .lead {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-neutral-800);
    margin-top: 0;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .legal-root strong {
    color: var(--color-neutral-900);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .legal-root code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    background: var(--color-neutral-100);
    padding: 1px 4px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    font-size: 0.92em;
  }
  .legal-root a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .footer-note {
    margin-top: 48px;
    padding-top: 16px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(55, 53, 47, 0.08);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
</style>
